<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2016/Carkeek-Original.jpg" alt="A plein air painting done at Carkeek Park" width="550" height="444" data-filename="Carkeek Shore.JPG" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Carkeek Shore (plein air). 8x10, oil on linen panel. 2016</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">&nbsp;I painted on the beach at Carkeek Park today. What a difference compared to my last visit - a rainy winter day when I had the whole place to myself.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">On a bright spring day like today, the colors of the PNW coast almost look artificial. I had to improvise a lot and gray down all my paint to make the sketch work. It was touch-and-go for a while with this painting and it nearly became a scraper. However, I managed to knuckle down and turn it around.</p>